# None of this is required to run `docker compose up` — every variable
# below is optional. Provider credentials (OpenAI, Gemini, Ollama, ...) are
# added from Settings > Providers in the dashboard after first login, and
# the encryption key that protects them at rest is generated automatically
# on first boot (see FLUXEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY below). Copy this file to .env
# only if you want to override one of these defaults, or for local
# (non-Docker) development of cmd/fluxen and fluxenctl.

# Deployment label, no behavioral effect.
FLUXEN_ENV=development

# Address the combined fluxen binary listens on.
HTTP_ADDR=:8080

# One of: debug, info, warn, error.
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Required. Standard PostgreSQL connection string.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://fluxen:fluxen@localhost:5432/fluxen?sslmode=disable

# Required. Standard Redis connection string.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# Optional. A deployment-wide OpenAI API key, set here instead of through
# Settings > Providers in the dashboard. Neither is required to boot —
# without either, /v1/chat/completions returns 503 no_provider_credential
# until a credential exists one way or the other.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Overrides the OpenAI API base URL — only useful for pointing
# the gateway at a mock server in local development/testing.
FLUXEN_OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3002

# Optional. Enables Gemini traffic through the gateway (Phase 7) when set.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Enables Ollama traffic through the gateway (Phase 7) when set
# — point it at a running Ollama instance, e.g. http://localhost:11434 or
# a Docker Compose service name.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=

# Optional. Base64-encoded 32-byte key (e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`)
# that encrypts Settings > Providers' stored credentials at rest. Leave
# this unset and Fluxen generates one itself on first boot, persisting it
# to FLUXEN_DATA_DIR — set this only if you want to manage the key
# yourself (e.g. injected by a secrets manager).
# FLUXEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Optional. Directory cmd/fluxen persists small local state to — today,
# just the auto-generated encryption key above. Defaults to /data, which
# docker-compose.yml backs with its own named volume.
# FLUXEN_DATA_DIR=

# Optional. The browser origin the control API allows to make credentialed
# cross-origin requests (CORS). Defaults to http://localhost:3000, which
# matches the dashboard's default compose port.
FLUXEN_DASHBOARD_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Optional. Set to "true" once you put TLS in front of Fluxen (a reverse
# proxy terminating HTTPS) so the session cookie is marked Secure. Leave
# unset/false for a plain-HTTP deployment — a Secure cookie is simply
# never sent to the browser over HTTP, which would break login.
# FLUXEN_COOKIE_SECURE=true
